# Human gates

The user is the gate at **every** stage. Do not chain stages in one turn.

After each stage, stop and wait for an explicit proceed (e.g. "accept", "implement", "review", "plan", "apply").

Never skip ahead: no Terraform in an architecture turn; no `terraform apply` in an implement turn; no commit unless they ask.

Stages (stop after each):

1. Intent / constraints
2. Architecture (ADR) — architect agent
3. Implementation plan (files to touch, no edits yet)
4. Implementation (code only)
5. Review (terraform-reviewer / security-auditor / cost-reviewer)
6. `terraform plan` (terraform-plan skill)
7. `terraform apply` (they confirm; hook also asks)

If unsure whether they approved, ask. Do not infer yes from silence.
